{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792708610998,"sessionID":"ses_e9a3e3dc5ffehVEX42a1T4uMqE","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_isw6dpiz","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/tmp/agent_opt_scratch/sw_16k__coding_03_compress_gen__09/work/compress.md"},"output":"<path>/tmp/agent_opt_scratch/sw_16k__coding_03_compress_gen__09/work/compress.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # compress_string coding exercise\n2: \n3: **Requirements:**\n4: \n5: Write a C function `void compress_string(const char *src, char *dest)` that performs basic run-length compression on an input string. \n6: \n7: Requirements:\n8: 1. Replace consecutive repeated characters with the character followed by the count (e.g., \"aabccc\" -> \"a2b1c3\").\n9: 2. Assume the input contains only alphabetical characters (a-z, A-Z) and is null-terminated.\n10: 3. Assume `dest` has sufficient allocated space to store the result.\n11: 4. Output the null-terminated compressed string into `dest`.\n12: \n13: Example:\n14: Input: \"aabcccccaaa\"\n15: Output: \"a2b1c5a3\"\n\n(End of file - total 15 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# compress_string coding exercise\n\n**Requirements:**\n\nWrite a C function `void compress_string(const char *src, char *dest)` that performs basic run-length compression on an input string. \n\nRequirements:\n1. Replace consecutive repeated characters with the character followed by the count (e.g., \"aabccc\" -> \"a2b1c3\").\n2. Assume the input contains only alphabetical characters (a-z, A-Z) and is null-terminated.\n3. Assume `dest` has sufficient allocated space to store the result.\n4. Output the null-terminated compressed string into `dest`.\n\nExample:\nInput: \"aabcccccaaa\"\nOutput: \"a2b1c5a3\"","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/tmp/agent_opt_scratch/sw_16k__coding_03_compress_gen__09/work/compress.md","text":"# compress_string coding exercise\n\n**Requirements:**\n\nWrite a C function `void compress_string(const char *src, char *dest)` that performs basic run-length compression on an input string. \n\nRequirements:\n1. Replace consecutive repeated characters with the character followed by the count (e.g., \"aabccc\" -> \"a2b1c3\").\n2. Assume the input contains only alphabetical characters (a-z, A-Z) and is null-terminated.\n3. Assume `dest` has sufficient allocated space to store the result.\n4. Output the null-terminated compressed string into `dest`.\n\nExample:\nInput: \"aabcccccaaa\"\nOutput: \"a2b1c5a3\"","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":15,"totalLines":15,"truncated":false}},"title":"tmp/agent_opt_scratch/sw_16k__coding_03_compress_gen__09/work/compress.md","time":{"start":1792708610982,"end":1792708610994}},"id":"prt_165c28b9f0017OY3BKORvaECi0","sessionID":"ses_e9a3e3dc5ffehVEX42a1T4uMqE","messageID":"msg_165c26a54001AVOzzmuWj26SYj"}}
